## Getting started

```bash
uv sync            # install dependencies from uv.lock
make hooks         # install the pre-commit hooks
uv run python scripts/rumbo_check.py   # the whole harness must be green (offline, no credentials needed)
```
{{#llm}}

Model calls happen only in `make evals-live`{{#claude_code}}, through the `claude` CLI with your own login{{/claude_code}}{{^claude_code}}, which needs `{{sdk_env_key}}` (copy `.env.example` to `.env`; use a development key with a spending limit){{/claude_code}}. In CI, only the nightly workflow holds that credential.
{{/llm}}

## Working with the agent

Open Claude Code here and say *"Read AGENTS.md and RUMBO.md; let's start phase R"*, or use
the commands `/rumbo-r`, `/rumbo-u`, `/rumbo-m`, `/rumbo-ancla`, `/rumbo-review`, `/rumbo-o`,
`/rumbo-gate` and `/rumbo-tour`. The check runs the same on Windows, macOS and Linux (`make check` is an optional alias). The `rumbo` CLI is available as `make rumbo ARGS="gate G4"`
(or install it: `uv tool install git+https://github.com/padillacm/RUMBO`).

`.claude/settings.json` pre-approves the harness commands and wires `scripts/rumbo_guard.py`
as hooks: the agent cannot edit the Makefile, `pyproject.toml`, CI, infra or the sensors,
cannot remove a template mark or bypass the tests, and cannot finish with the check red.
When it is blocked it asks you; you edit those files by hand. Replace `@your-handle` in
`.github/CODEOWNERS` and the contact in `SECURITY.md`.

## Layout

| Folder | What lives there |
|---|---|
| `src/{{package}}/domain` | pure logic (no I/O) |
| `src/{{package}}/app` | use cases; depends only on `domain` |
| `src/{{package}}/adapters` | external APIs, databases, LLM |
| `src/{{package}}/api` | FastAPI / CLI |
| `tests/{unit,property,integration,architecture}` | sensors |
| `docs/` | brief, PRD, ADRs, C4, threat model, runbook, SLOs, decisions, reviews |
| `specs/` | EARS specs per feature |
| `spikes/` | throwaway code; never imported from `src/` |
